{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_007: multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, weighted fusion → 52.3% acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether the multimodal fusion is actually adding value over the image modality alone. config_002 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest possible comparison: it holds the image encoder (resnet50) and profile setting (singleprofile) identical to config_007 while removing the RNA branch entirely. If image-only performance is close to or exceeds 52.3%, the current RNA encoding (pca_n2000) with weighted fusion is not contributing, and future effort should target better RNA representations or fusion strategies. If image-only is substantially lower, multimodal fusion is confirmed as beneficial and we can then efficiently explore fusion type, aggregation, and encoder upgrades. Resolving this fundamental question before varying fusion, aggregation, or encoders avoids wasting budget on secondary design choices while the primary 'does multimodal help?' question remains unanswered."
}

